sentences.l:
So now, if a god, making trial, should come here,
do not you at all with the immortal gods straight on fight,
the others;

then indeed thrice as much might took hold of him, like a lion
which a shepherd on the farm over his fleecy sheep
may graze as it leaps over the yard, and not subdue;

and to their father lament and grievous sorrows
he left, since not living, from the battle having come home,
he received them;

And him Aeneas saw laying waste the ranks of men,
and set out to go up through the battle and through the turmoil of spears
seeking godlike Pandarus, in case anywhere he might find him;

But come, at this man shoot a shaft, to Zeus your hands raising,
whoever this is who prevails, and has already done many evils
to the Trojans, since the knees of many and good men he has loosed;

at once then from me let my head a foreign man cut off,
if I do not this bow in the shining fire put,
breaking it with my hands;
